Subject: [PATCH 1/2] SYCL: FA TILE, phantom heads and padded GQA for small batches

The TILE kernel packs ncols2 Q heads of one KV head per work-group, but it
derives the KV head as head0 / gqa_ratio, so ncols2 must divide the GQA ratio.
For G = 3, 5, 6 and 7, dispatch therefore falls back to ncols2 = 1 or 2 and
streams each KV head's K/V up to G times. This includes F16 single-token
decode on such models.

This patch uses KV-head-major work-group indexing, as CUDA's MMA kernel does,
and masks phantom heads:
- zero Q;
- no sink read;
- no output or dst_meta write.
When ncols2 divides G the mapping is identical to before. For non-power-of-two
G < 8, while tokens * next_pow2(G) <= GGML_SYCL_FATTN_TILE_PAD_MAX_COLS (32),
dispatch then pads ncols2 to next_pow2(G), so K/V is streamed once. It adds no
new template instances. DV = 512 is unchanged.

Tested on: Intel OpenCL CPU device only (correctness). A770 timing not run.

